WEBVTT

00:09:58.832 --> 00:10:02.459
because I think the founders and CEOs
have a bit more agency in those things,

00:10:02.483 --> 00:10:05.691
and that wasn't the person
paying the bills,

00:10:05.715 --> 00:10:08.000
this was someone
who worked in the building

00:10:08.024 --> 00:10:11.765
and that the community team
took such good care of this person,

00:10:11.789 --> 00:10:13.046
and they didn't need to,

00:10:13.070 --> 00:10:15.723
again, this person
wasn't, like, the direct customer.

00:10:16.429 --> 00:10:18.408
And that by being part of that community,

00:10:18.432 --> 00:10:20.907
that person was taken care of.

00:10:21.698 --> 00:10:23.162
That really meant a lot to me,

00:10:23.186 --> 00:10:27.140
and I thought that that
was really beautiful.

00:10:27.164 --> 00:10:30.903
A group of people that could be
looking out for each other.